# Degree-one places of `L(E)` and the geometry of `E(L)`: reusable interface

This module is the standalone, reusable export of the "degree-one place / point valuation" theory
of the `Work.MotC2` chapter (audit node C2, step (i)).  It is intended to be imported by other
subprojects (for instance the `MotV` route) that need the correspondence
"rational places of `L(E)/L` ↦ rational points of `E`" without redoing the commutative algebra.

## What is here

Vocabulary (all in namespace `Work.MotC2`, defined in `Submission/Work/MotC2/Defs.lean`):

* `Coord E` = `L[X,Y]/(W_E)` is the affine coordinate ring, `Func E = FractionRing (Coord E)` the
  function field `L(E)`.
* `genX E = x`, `genY E = y` are the images of `X`, `Y`; `baseE E` is `E` over `L(E)`.
* `affRing E` is `L[x,y] ⊆ L(E)`, the affine coordinate ring as a subalgebra.
* `infCoordRing E = L[1/x, y/x²]` is the chart-at-infinity coordinate ring, `infIdeal E` its
  maximal ideal `(1/x, y/x²)`, and `infPlace E` its localization: the local ring of the point at
  infinity `O`.  (`infU E = 1/x`, `infW E = y/x²`; `infW E` is the uniformizer.)
* `affPlaceAt E a b` is the local ring of the affine rational point `(a, b)`, i.e. the localization
  of `Coord E` at `⟨x - a, y - b⟩`.
* `IsRatPlace E S` says that the subalgebra `S ⊆ L(E)` is a *rational place* of `L(E)/L`: a
  discrete valuation ring whose residue field is `L` via the structure map, whose fraction field is
  `L(E)` (equivalently: the local ring of an `L`-rational point of the projective curve).

Main results (each in its own module, imported below):

* `Work.MotC2.Relations` — the Weierstrass relation in `Coord E`, in `L(E)` and in the
  chart-at-infinity coordinates, plus nonsingularity (`Equation → Nonsingular`).
* `Work.MotC2.Integral` — `genY E` is integral over `L[genX E]`, `infW E` integral over
  `L[infU E]` (so a place containing `x` contains `y`, and one containing `1/x` contains `y/x²`).
* `Work.MotC2.InfPlace` — `infPlace E` is a rational place, with maximal ideal generated by
  `infW E`, whose non-units are the multiples of `infW E`.
* `Work.MotC2.AffPlace` — for a nonsingular point `(a,b)`, `affPlaceAt E a b` is a rational place,
  and it is the localization of `Coord E` at `⟨x - a, y - b⟩`.
* `Work.MotC2.DVRMaximal` — a rational place is maximal among DVR subalgebras of `L(E)`.
* `Work.MotC2.Classification` — **every rational place of `L(E)/L` is `infPlace E` or
  `affPlaceAt E a b` for a unique nonsingular point `(a,b)`**: `E(L) ∪ {O}`.
* `Work.MotC2.PoleOrder` — `𝓛(2O) = ⟨1, x⟩` and `𝓛(3O) = ⟨1, x, y⟩` on the coordinate ring
  (as the `r ↔ r·infW² ∈ infPlace E` and `r ↔ r·infW³ ∈ infPlace E` criteria).
-/

